</form></div>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap split" style="gap:80px">
  <div><p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 20px">Does this sound like you?</p><h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,58px);margin:0">Signs it's time to work on the website.</h2></div>
  <div><div style="display:flex;gap:18px;padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><span class="red label" style="min-width:34px">01</span><p class="p" style="font-size:18px;color:var(--ink)">Adding a product or page takes too long.</p></div><div style="display:flex;gap:18px;padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><span class="red label" style="min-width:34px">02</span><p class="p" style="font-size:18px;color:var(--ink)">Plugins or apps keep clashing with each other.</p></div><div style="display:flex;gap:18px;padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><span class="red label" style="min-width:34px">03</span><p class="p" style="font-size:18px;color:var(--ink)">The site works on desktop but is awkward on phones.</p></div><div style="display:flex;gap:18px;padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><span class="red label" style="min-width:34px">04</span><p class="p" style="font-size:18px;color:var(--ink)">Payments, shipping or your CRM are patched together.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 20px">How we work</p>
  <h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,58px);margin:0 0 56px;max-width:820px">Review, plan, then price. In that order.</h2>
  <div class="g3"><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 01</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Scope</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">We confirm the platform, the features and the integrations, in a written plan.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 02</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Build</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Theme or custom code, tested on phones, tablets and desktops.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 03</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Launch</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">A checked release, with a handover so your team knows how to run it.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
  <div style="background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:26px;padding:50px">
    <p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 18px">What changes</p>
    <p class="p" style="font-size:20px;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 18px">A site that is stable, easy to change and connected to the tools you already use.</p>
    <a href="/web-development" class="label red">See how we work &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section data-expansion style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
<h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,52px);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:860px">How we build and change your store</h2>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">A well-built store is stable, fast and easy to change. A poorly built one breaks when an app updates, takes days to add a product and needs a developer for every small change. We build with the second problem in mind.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">What we build</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 26px;padding-left:22px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink2)"><li style="margin:0 0 8px">New stores on Shopify, BigCommerce, WooCommerce, Magento and WordPress.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">Custom sections and features that your theme or platform doesn't include.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">Connections to payments, shipping, your accounting tools and your customer systems.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">Migrations from one platform to another, planned so that URLs and rankings are kept.</li></ul>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">How we keep the build safe</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We test each part on phones, tablets and desktops before launch. We keep changes in a test copy of the store, so the live site isn't changed until the work has been checked. Every project ends with a handover: what was built, how it works and how to make simple changes yourself.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">Why this matters for search</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">A store that breaks, loads slowly or changes its URLs without planning loses rankings. The way a store is built affects how search engines read it, so development and SEO are planned together.</p>
<h3 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(32px,3.6vw,44px);margin:56px 0 24px">Frequently asked questions</h3>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--ink);margin:0 0 20px"><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Can you work on a store we already have?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Yes. We'll review the current build first, then agree what to change.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Do you build apps?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Where a store needs a feature that existing apps don't cover, we can build a custom solution. We'll recommend an existing app when one does the job well.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">What happens after launch?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">You can keep us on for upkeep, or hand over with documentation. The choice is yours, and it's part of the plan we agree before the work starts.</p></details></div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap">
  <div style="background:var(--red);color:#fff;border-radius:36px;padding:clamp(60px,8vw,100px) clamp(24px,5vw,60px)">
    <h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(40px,7vw,88px);margin:0 0 26px;max-width:900px">Not sure what your site needs?</h2>
